  "name": "Example: Finding a Height Corresponding to an Extended Base",
  "problem": "Consider the triangle $ABC$ shown below. Construct the height corresponding to $\\overline{BC}.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13945712/assets/72b40526cafc5d1db902ea9947a2808020dfadcf6a84238e8e3a2459ca95fe07.png)",
  "worked_solution": "The height (or altitude) corresponding to $\\overline{BC}$ is a line segment that \n\n- runs from the opposite vertex $A$ to the line $\\overset{\\longleftrightarrow}{BC},$ and\n\n- is perpendicular to $\\overset{\\longleftrightarrow}{BC}.$\n\nTo draw the height, we proceed as follows:\n\n- Extend the line segment $\\overline{BC}.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13945712/assets/010d2c4de6c3df93112295eb2351247c2162a0d84a1f6e122fdca71dca72c168.png)\n\n- Draw the perpendicular from $A$ to $\\overset{\\longleftrightarrow}{BC}.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13945712/assets/392d7d23590557ccce29b25cecabb276ee875f86c172ce15c845c13668939933.png)",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "result": null,
